<task id="001" project="spaarkeai-compose-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Spike 1 — Action row + structured OutputSchemaJson reliability</title>
    <phase>0 Spikes</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>4</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>000</dependencies>
    <blocks>040, 041, 042, 043, 044</blocks>
    <tags>ai, azure-openai, dataverse</tags>
    <rigor-hint>STANDARD</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Exploratory spike — throwaway prompt/schema experiment recorded as a spike note, not production catalog rows. STANDARD per TASK-INDEX.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Prompt + schema validation experiment over the shipped seam; no architectural blast radius. Sonnet per TASK-INDEX.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>W0b</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Prove that a single R2 Action row (e.g. compose-explain-clause) with an adeu-style behavioral prompt (SystemPrompt) and a structured OutputSchemaJson returns schema-valid JSON reliably when dispatched through the shipped seam validated in Spike 0. The goal is to lock the prompt-pattern, the JPS scope `description` format ("tool descriptions ARE the prompt"), and the Action schema shape (OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator-compliant — no property-level boolean `required`) before Phase 4 authors 5 real catalog rows. Run enough sample selections to characterise reliability; record failure modes and the schema/prompt adjustments that fix them. All artifacts are throwaway; the deliverable is a spike note.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Prompt engineer + AI platform developer fluent in JPS (JSON Prompt Schema) Action authoring, OutputSchemaJson / OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator constraints (ADR-039), and adeu's "tool descriptions are the prompt" pattern.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A spike note at projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/notes/spikes/spike-1-action-schema.md that unlocks the Phase-4 decision: the validated prompt pattern, JPS scope description format, and Action schema shape that returns schema-valid JSON reliably. It records a measured reliability figure across sample selections and the exact OutputSchemaJson/SystemPrompt shape to copy in Phase 4.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §13 Spike 1 + §7 (Action + Binding authoring) + §2.0 (tool descriptions surface as user hints). Phase 4 authors 5 Action+Binding pairs; this spike de-risks the Action-half prompt+schema pattern once, so all five reuse a proven shape. Decision unlocked (design §13): prompt-pattern validation; JPS scope description format; Action schema shape. Builds directly on Spike 0's confirmed dispatch seam.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file purpose="dispatch-seam">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/dispatchConsumer.ts — the seam Spike 0 validated; reuse to invoke the Action</file>
      <file purpose="catalog-mirror">infra/dataverse/inputschemas/ — mirror-first Action + Binding rows (throwaway)</file>
      <file purpose="spike-0-note">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/notes/spikes/spike-0-dispatch-path.md — the confirmed seam contract this spike builds on</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="000" status="not-started">Requires the Spike-0 confirmed dispatch seam to invoke the Action row.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">Action row carries the prompt (SystemPrompt + OutputSchemaJson + Temperature + ModelDeploymentId); OutputSchemaJson MUST be OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator-compliant — property-level boolean `required` is BANNED. Rows are mirror-first under infra/dataverse/inputschemas/. No new dispatch endpoint; dispatch via the shipped seam.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-040">Dispatched output is ledger-written; the spike reuses that path, does not bypass it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Throwaway experiment — the Action/Binding rows are not the final Phase-4 rows; deliverable is a spike note recording the reusable pattern.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>ai/jps-action-authoring, ai/output-schema-validation</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-040-session-ledger.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + load">Load this task, project CLAUDE.md, Spike-0 note, and the knowledge files.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Author Action + prompt">Author a throwaway Action row with an adeu-style SystemPrompt and a structured OutputSchemaJson (validator-compliant). Draft the JPS scope description in the "description = prompt = tooltip" format.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Dispatch samples">Invoke the Action over several representative clause selections through the Spike-0 seam.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Measure reliability">Record how often responses are schema-valid; capture failure modes (missing fields, extra prose, invalid enum) and the prompt/schema tweaks that fix them.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Write spike note">Record the validated prompt pattern, JPS scope description format, and Action schema shape for Phase 4 reuse.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="notes" ephemeral="true">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/notes/spikes/spike-1-action-schema.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">Spike note documents a validated prompt pattern, JPS scope `description` format, and Action schema shape — the decision the spike unlocks (design §13).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A measured reliability figure (schema-valid rate across sample selections) is recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The OutputSchemaJson shape is OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator-compliant with no property-level boolean `required` (ADR-039), and the note states this.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Failure modes + their prompt/schema fixes are captured for Phase-4 reuse.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
